@ENDNODE

@NODE Usage "Usage And Examples - © 1995 by bObO/MYSTiC"

   The  usage  of  MultiTop  is very simple, and it is the only thing you
   have to "learn", if you don't want to make your own designs!

   Usage: MULTITOP <designfile> <outputfile> [<userdata>] [UKEYS <file>]
                   [CONFDB <file>] [NOANSI]

   <designfile> : Full path to your designfile. You may use AMIGADOS
                  wildcards to use random design files. (ie #?)

   <outputfile> : Full path to your outputfile. You may use an asterisk
                  for output directly to screen. (i.e. "*")

   [<userdata>] : Full path to your userdata.  (BBS:User.data is default)

   [UKEYS <file>]  : The  Userkeys file  is  ONLY  used if the designfile
                     need  cps  rates  info.  <file>  is the full path to
                     your userkeys file. (BBS:User.keys is default).

   [CONFDB <file>] : If  you  have  conference accounting activated,  you
                     can  use  conference database to make the bulletins.
                     <file>  is  the  full  path to your conf.db file for
                     that conference.

   [NOANSI] : Write a NO ANSI output. (Ansi is default)


   Some examples:
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   MULTITOP Designs/MTopULBytes#?.dsg BBS:Bull.txt SYS:User.data NOANSI
   --- Generate a random TOP UPLOADERS bulletin using SYS:User.data with
       NOANSI to BBS:Bull.txt

   MULTITOP Designs/MTopULBytes#?.dsg BBS:Bull.txt CONFDB BBS:Conf2/Conf.db
   --- Generate a random TOP UPLOADERS bulletin from conference 2 to
       BBS:Bull.txt

   MULTITOP Designs/MTopDLBytes#?.dsg BBS:Bull.txt UKEYS SYS:User.keys
   --- Generate a random TOP DOWNLOADERS bulletin using a external Userkeys
       to BBS:Bull.txt

   MULTITOP Designs/MTopMsgs1.dsg * NOANSI
   --- Generate a TOP MESSAGES bulletin (design 1) with NOANSI directly to
       screen.
@ENDNODE

@NODE DesignGeneral "General Info about the Design files - © 1995 bObO/MST"

   As  you  probably already figured out, MultiTop needs a design file to
   work.   A  designfile is a normal textfile (ASCII) created in a normal
   text-editor  with  some keywords in it.  The designfiles can also have
   its personal config in it.  (explained later)

   PLEASE NOTE

   You  don't have to make your own design if you don't have time or want
   to.   There are many nice designs delivered with this archive that you
   can  freely  use, so if you aren't that good at painting etc, just use
   them.   (This  means  that  you  DON'T have to read the part about the
   design files)
@ENDNODE

@NODE DesignKeywords "How to create your own files - © 1995 bObO/MST"

   I  recommend  you  to take a look at the included example design-files
   while reading this chapter to understand how it works.


   LIST OF AVAILABLE KEYWORDS

   USERINFO               BOARDINFO
   ~~~~~~~~               ~~~~~~~~~
   UN=UserName            TC=Total Calls
   LT=Location            TM=Total Msgs
   UB=Uploaded Bytes      UB=Total Uploaded Bytes
   UK=Uploaded K          UK=Total Uploaded K
   UM=Uploaded Megs       UM=Total Uploaded Megs
   UF=Uploaded Files      UF=Total Uploaded Files
   DB=Downloaded Bytes    DB=Total Downloaded Bytes
   DK=Downloaded K        DK=Total Downloaded K
   DM=Downloaded Megs     DM=Total Downloaded Megs
   DF=Downloaded Files    DF=Total Downloaded Files
   UC=Upload CPS Record   SC=System Calls
   DC=Download CPS Record TU=Total Active Users
   MS=Messages            LT=Last Updated (Time)
   CS=Calls               LD=Last Updated (Date)
   ST=Status              RG=Register Information
   ---------------------- VT=Version Text

   NOTE: The keyword VT *MUST* be used, or no output will be written.
         It will insert a string (MultiTop v2.1) of 14 chars long.


   USERINFO format:
   %<pos><center><length><keyword>  Example: %01-10UN
   |  |     |       |       |
   |  |     |       |       |> Userinfo Keyword
   |  |     |       |--------> Number of chars to display of keyword
   |  |     |----------------> Minus (-) for left, dot (.) for right
   |  |----------------------> User number from top
   |-------------------------> Keyword Identifer

   BOARDINFO format:
   %<center><length><keyword>       Example: %-10VT
   |   |       |       |
   |   |       |       |-----> Boardinfo Keyword
   |   |       |-------------> Number of chars to display of keyword
   |   |---------------------> Minus (-) for left, dot (.) for right
   |-------------------------> Keyword Identifer

   Examples
   ~~~~~~~~
   Username: [%01-10UN]  Location: [%01.10LT]  Bytes: [%01-10UB]

   The above string would be translated to:
   Username: [bObO/mYSTi]  Location: [    mYStiC]  Bytes: [1,123,123 ]


   Total uploaded bytes: [%-10UB]  files: [%.00UF]

   The above string would be translated to:
   Total uploaded bytes: [1,123,123]  files: [1,123]

                                PLEASE NOTE!

   All  I  want from you who make the design, is NOT to remove or somehow
   hide  the  VT-keyword.   I  KNOW there is quite an easy way to hide it
   with esc- chars (i.e.  set the black color before the keyword) or such
   things, but PLEASE show me some respect for my work and leave it as it
   should be - thank you.

       (THIS IS ALL I ASK FROM YOU. YOU DON'T HAVE TO INCLUDE MY NAME OR
        OTHER THINGS, THE VT-KEYWORD IS ENOUGH)

   See also: @{"Configuring Designer Files" link DesignPersonalSettings}

@ENDNODE

@NODE DesignPersonalSettings "Personal Settings in Designer Files - © 1995 bObO/MST"

   The  design  file(s)  may  have  its  own  config  in  it.  All of the
   following  keywords  for setting options are optional, but if you want
   to  make  an  other  output  then  top  ulbytes, you need to use them.
   Available commands/settings are:

   SEPARATOR=DOT    - Use DOT (.) separator
             COMMA  - Use COMMA (,) separator
             NONE   - Donot use any separator

   READUSERKEYS - Read userkeys when using this design - to be able to use
                  cps rates information.

   SORT=UPLOADEDBYTES    - Sort userlist by Uploaded Bytes (DEFAULT)
        UPLOADEDFILES    - Sort userlist by Uploaded Files
        DOWNLOADEDBYTES  - Sort userlist by Downloaded Bytes
        DOWNLOADEDFILES  - Sort userlist by Downloaded Files
        CALLS            - Sort userlist by Calls
        MESSAGES         - Sort userlist by Messages
        UPLOADCPS        - Sort userlist by Upload CPS
        DOWNLOADCPS      - Sort userlist by Download CPS

   All lines in the designfile starting with '@' will *NOT* be written in
   the output. @ followed by an option will activate it. You may also use
   @ to write comments in the designfile.


   EXAMPLES
   ~~~~~~~~
   @ This is a comment line

   @SEPARATOR=DOT                   I can write whatever i want out here!

   @SORT=DOWNLOADEDBYTES            I can write whatever i want out here!


   For more help and examples, take a look at the included designfiles.
@ENDNODE

@NODE ConfigProgram "Config Program - © 1995 bObO/MST"

   MultiTop  has  a built-in config program where you configure MultiTop.
   I  wont  go  into  details  what  every option does, because it's very
   intuitive to use.  Go and see.

   To  start  the  config program, write "MULTITOP CFG" at the prompt, or
   start MultiTop from workbench.

   NOTE: If you don't have your userdata located in the default path
         (BBS:), you may enter "MULTITOP CFG <userdata>"

     IE: MULTITOP CFG SYS:USER.DATA
@ENDNODE

